---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const updated = new Date(`${siteConfig.privacyLastUpdated}T00:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Trillian handles your data: sessions and your driver name are stored only on your phone, location is used only while you record, and there is no account, server, analytics or internet permission."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy policy">
    The short version: your laps stay on your phone. Trillian has no account, no server, no
    analytics and no tracking.
  </PageHero>

  <div class="container--narrow prose policy">
    <p class="small muted">
      Last updated: <time datetime={siteConfig.privacyLastUpdated}>{updated}</time>. Applies to the
      current release of the Trillian Android app and to this website.
    </p>

    <Callout tone="free" title="In plain language">
      <ul>
        <li>Everything you record is stored in the app’s private storage on your phone.</li>
        <li>
          The app does not hold Android’s internet permission, so it cannot send your data anywhere.
        </li>
        <li>Nothing leaves your phone unless you choose to share it.</li>
      </ul>
    </Callout>

    <h2 id="stored">What the app stores</h2>
    <p>Stored locally on your phone, in the app’s private storage:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your driver name</strong> — the name you enter at first launch (no email, password or
        account).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sessions and laps</strong> — session names, track details, lap and sector times.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Coaching insights</strong> generated from your sessions.</li>
      <li><strong>Saved circuits</strong> — start/finish lines you choose to save.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Telemetry recordings</strong> — GPS position, speed and heading, and phone motion data
        captured during a session.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      All analysis — lap detection, sectors, charts, track maps and coaching — runs on your phone.
    </p>

    <h2 id="network">Network, servers and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The current release of Trillian has <strong
        >no server, no account system, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking</strong
      >. The app does not request Android’s internet permission, so it cannot transmit your data. It
      works fully in flight mode.
    </p>
    <p class="small muted">
      Accounts and cloud backup are planned for a future version. If that changes how data is
      handled, this policy will be updated before such a release.
    </p>

    <h2 id="permissions">Permissions</h2>
    <h3>Location (required)</h3>
    <p>
      Location is needed to record your position on track. Choose <em>While using the app</em>.
      Trillian never tracks you in the background: location is sampled only during a session you
      started yourself, with a notification visible the whole time. Opening the app also starts
      finding satellites so your GPS is ready at the track; this stops when you leave the app.
      Trillian never asks for “Allow all the time”.
    </p>
    <h3>Notifications (optional)</h3>
    <p>
      Used to show recording status and the “GPS signal lost” warning. Recording works normally if
      you decline.
    </p>
    <p>Trillian does not request Physical Activity permission.</p>

    <h2 id="sharing">When you share</h2>
    <p>
      Data leaves your phone only when you choose to share it — for example, a <strong
        >share card</strong
      > image showing your best lap, session date, track and driver name. You pick the app it goes to
      (messages, social apps, gallery), and that app’s own privacy terms then apply. Sharing never changes,
      moves or deletes your recorded data.
    </p>

    <h2 id="delete">Deleting your data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>One session:</strong> long-press it on the Home screen and choose Delete. This removes
        its laps, coaching insights and telemetry file.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Everything:</strong> Profile → Clear User Data → Delete everything.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Or</strong> clear the app’s storage in Android Settings, or uninstall Trillian.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Because nothing is uploaded, there is no server copy — and no backup. Deletion is permanent.
    </p>

    <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
    <p>
      This website uses <strong>no cookies, no analytics and no third-party trackers</strong>, and
      it loads no external fonts or scripts. It is hosted on GitHub Pages; like any web host, GitHub
      may process technical data such as IP addresses to deliver and secure the site — see the
      <a
        href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
        rel="noopener">GitHub Privacy Statement</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, email
      <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
    <p><a href={url('/faq/#data')}>Data &amp; privacy FAQ →</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    padding-top: var(--sp-6);
  }
  .policy h2 {
    margin-top: var(--sp-7);
  }
</style>
